    // After-trial section
    pricingAfterTrialTitle: "What changes after the 14-day trial",
    pricingAfterTrialBody: "Nothing dramatic. You stay signed in, your data is safe, every feature is still there. Free is genuinely usable — these are the only caps that come back when the trial ends:",
    pricingAfterTrialCap1: "200 sales logged per month",
    pricingAfterTrialCap2: "100 expenses logged per month",
    pricingAfterTrialCap3: "10 receipt OCR scans per month",
    pricingAfterTrialCap4: "30 AI Copilot questions per day",
    pricingAfterTrialCap5: "Top 5 active AI insights at a time",
    pricingAfterTrialCap6: "1 vertical module (pick one)",
    pricingAfterTrialCap7: "90 days of full history (older stays read-only)",
    pricingAfterTrialCap8: "1 business, 1 user",
    pricingAfterTrialClosing: "No card needed to start the trial — it auto-runs when you sign up. You only enter a card if you click \"Lock in founding rate\" to keep your founding price (Starter 129 kr/mo or Pro 249 kr/mo) for life. Otherwise the trial just ends and you drop to Free.",
    // FAQ
    faqHeading: "Common questions",
    faqQ1: "What happens when my 14-day trial ends?",
    faqA1: "It depends on whether you locked in. If you did NOT lock in: you drop to Free automatically. Every feature stays, only the usage caps come back, your data is untouched, and you're never charged. If you DID lock in (clicked 'Lock in founding rate' and added a card): your card is charged the founding rate (Starter 129 kr/mo or Pro 249 kr/mo) on day 15 and monthly after, locked at the founding rate for life. Either way: no surprises — the trial banner counts the days down, and you choose.",
    faqQ2: "Why does Free have every feature, just with caps?",
    faqA2: "Because feature-gating is a tax on small shops. A side-business owner shouldn't be locked out of AI insights just because they only do 50 sales a month — they need the insights MORE than a busy shop does. Caps mean Free users get full value, and only upgrade when they've actually outgrown what Free can support.",
    faqQ3: "How does the founding-member price work?",
    faqA3: "The first 100 Pro subscribers lock in 249 kr/mo for as long as they stay subscribed — even when our regular Pro price kicks in at 349 kr/mo. Cancel and rejoin? You'd pay regular price. Stay subscribed continuously? You're locked in.",
    faqQ4: "I run a chain with multiple branches — what fits?",
    faqA4: "Pro covers up to 3 locations. For more, email hello@bonbox.dk and we'll quote a custom Business plan within 1 business day.",
    faqQ5: "Is BonBox a Dinero alternative?",
    faqA5: "No. BonBox is not a registered digital bookkeeping system, so you keep what you have — and you keep paying for it. BonBox does the daily work: fakturaer, customers, mileage, receipts read by OCR and bank matching, so there is less to sort out afterwards. The official filings, MOMS-angivelse and årsregnskab, still happen in your bookkeeping system, with your revisor.",
    faqQ6: "What about MOMS?",
    faqA6: "All prices shown are excl. MOMS. Danish businesses are invoiced with 25% MOMS automatically. EU businesses with valid MOMS numbers are reverse-charged.",
    faqQ7: "Can I cancel anytime?",
    faqA7: "Yes. No contracts, no notice period. You'll keep access until the end of the current billing period and can export all your data at any time.",
    faqQ8: "Is my data safe?",
    faqA8: "Your database is in Ireland. Receipt photos go to Anthropic in the US to be read — they are not kept and are not used to train models. Everything is encrypted at rest and in transit. We never sell your data and never hand it to marketers. Export and delete are built in, and every processor is named in the privacy policy.",
    faqQ9: "Is BonBox a registered digital bookkeeping system?",
    faqA9: "No — and we're upfront about it. BonBox is an invoicing + data-capture tool (kasserapport OCR, faktura, mileage, daily-close PDF). It is not registered with Erhvervsstyrelsen as a digital bogføringssystem under the 2024 Bookkeeping Act. If your business is legally required to keep books in a registered system, keep using Dinero / Billy / e-conomic for that — BonBox sits alongside it and feeds clean exports. We don't try to replace your revisor; we make their input cheaper.",
    faqQ10: "Does my revisor need their own login?",
    faqA10: "Yes — and it's free. From Profile → Revisor access, send your accountant an email invite. They get a read-only BonBox login: they can see fakturaer, daily closes, expenses, tax overview, and download PDFs/exports — but they can't change a single thing. Every action they take is audit-logged. No more password sharing, no GDPR risk, no \"forward me the PDF\" round trips. Revisor access is on Starter+ — Free can still send PDFs by email.",
    faqQ11: "How does the staff schedule autopilot work?",
    faqA11: "Pro feature. Open Staff → Schedule → Run autopilot. BonBox reads your last 8 weeks of revenue by day-of-week, joins it with the 7-day weather forecast for your city, then suggests a shift plan for next week that meets predicted demand at minimum labor cost. It respects DK labor law (45-min break for 6+ hour shifts, 11-hr daily rest, weekly hour caps) and each staff member's availability. You review the suggestion shift-by-shift, edit anything you want, then tap Apply. Most Copenhagen cafés save 5–10% on wages once the model has 2-3 weeks of data to learn from.",
    faqQ12: "How does bank reconciliation work?",
    faqA12: "Today: you upload your netbank CSV (2 clicks in Danske Bank, Nordea, Jyske, Spar Nord, or Lunar) and BonBox auto-matches payments to your open fakturaer with confidence tiers. High-confidence matches are one-tap to confirm; uncertain ones land in a review inbox instead of the books. Direct PSD2 sync (Aiia / Salt Edge) is on the roadmap once we close the partnership; the CSV path will stay as the fallback. We won't toggle it on until it's actually wired up — no fake 'Connected' badges.",
    pricingTrademarkNotice: "Dinero, Billy, e-conomic, MobilePay and Dankort are trademarks of their respective owners. BonBox is not affiliated with or endorsed by any of these companies. References are made for interoperability and comparative purposes under nominative fair use.",
    // Closer-prompt onboarding card — stakes the two-actor segment in the product flow
    closerPromptTitle: "Who closes for you?",
    closerPromptBody: "In most hospitality businesses, front-of-house staff close out at end of shift — not the owner. Tell us who's closing so they get the daily-close confirmation. (Owner still gets the consolidated PDF.)",
